`docs/HERMES_SOURCE_COMPARISON.json`; this file holds the exact
`wave3.overlay` hash replacements for the Wave 4 Qubit overlay edits so
they can be merged without an agent F edit to the JSON.

Wave 4 made **no edits to vendored `frontend/hermes-web/**` source** (the
vendored dashboard is byte-clean for the pinned revision except for the
already-documented Wave 1–3 patches). The only changed files are the
Qubit-owned overlay (`frontend/hermes-qubit/**`), whose hashes live under
`wave3.overlay` in the manifest.

Until the rows below are merged, 
`tests/test_branding_parity_wave3.py::test_overlay_manifest_hashes_are_valid`
reports the edited files as stale. That is expected provenance handoff, not
a functional regression; all Wave 1–3 functional/route/behaviour tests stay
green (`test_dashboard_plugin_fleet.py`, `test_dashboard_page_closure_wave2.py`,
`test_dashboard_branding_wave1.py`, `test_dashboard_ops8tf.py`,
`test_dashboard_agent3_plugins.py`, `test_hermes_vendor8tf.py`).

